{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5462870","formula":"C₂₂H₂₆FNO","hill":"C22H26FNO","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"F":1.0,"H":26.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Fluorophen"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fluorophen, or fluorofen, is a fluorinated analogue of phenazocine, an opioid drug of the benzomorphan group, which was developed as a radioligand for the purpose of labeling opioid receptors during PET scans (with 18F). Unlike most other benzomorphan derivatives, fluorophen acts as a full agonist of the opioid receptors with preferential affinity for the μ-opioid receptor (approximately 6x that of morphine), similar but slightly lower affinity for the δ-opioid receptor (equipotent to [D-Ala2, D-Leu5]enkephalin), and very low affinity for the κ-opioid receptor."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":3036297,"mass":339.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@H]1[C@@H]2CC3=C([C@@]1(CCN2CCC4=CC=C(C=C4)F)C)C=C(C=C3)O","inchikey":"PUPFATUGTIQBQA-UZQPLGKSSA-N","iupac":"(1R,9S,13R)-10-[2-(4-fluorophenyl)ethyl]-1,13-dimethyl-10-azatricyclo[7.3.1.02,7]trideca-2(7),3,5-trien-4-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3036297","atoms":51,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":7.674,"y":0.356,"z":-0.834,"el":"F"},{"x":-6.795,"y":0.683,"z":0.024,"el":"O"},{"x":0.263,"y":-0.906,"z":1.223,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.312,"y":-1.409,"z":-0.475,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.969,"y":-0.824,"z":-0.926,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.568,"y":-0.064,"z":0.37,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.942,"y":-2.299,"z":0.815,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.123,"y":1.353,"z":0.328,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.228,"y":-0.162,"z":-0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.386,"y":-2.272,"z":1.233,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.661,"y":1.145,"z":0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.909,"y":-2.311,"z":-1.568,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.951,"y":-0.029,"z":-2.239,"el":"C"},{"x":1.657,"y":-0.942,"z":0.818,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.623,"y":-0.287,